1
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:26,025
I'm sorry.
I am so sorry.

2
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,860
- Let me help you with that.
- It's okay, man.

3
00:00:27,985 --> 00:00:29,946
- Wait. Let... let me...
- It's fine. Just leave it.

4
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,602
I loved that movie.
Classic movies are the best.

5
00:01:01,727 --> 00:01:02,895
You fell asleep.

6
00:01:03,437 --> 00:01:05,231
That's how you can tell
I liked it.

7
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:12,446
So, listen, um, turns out my old band
is playing a gig downtown tonight.

8
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,949
- Do you wanna go?
- Your old band? You were in a band?

9
00:01:15,074 --> 00:01:18,119
- I never told you I was in a band?
- No, no. What did you play?

10
00:01:18,744 --> 00:01:23,291
- Bass. Vocals.
- Ah, you are so cool.

11
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:24,875
- Let's go.
- Yeah?

12
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:26,877
- Yeah.
- Okay, then. We need a cab.

13
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:34,176
Hey.

14
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,762
About that question.

15
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:42,310
Was that "do you like butter with your
popcorn" or "will you come with me to D.C."?

16
00:01:42,643 --> 00:01:43,686
D.C.

17
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:47,773
Oh, I just wanted you to know
I've been thinking about it really hard

18
00:01:47,898 --> 00:01:50,318
and I-I wanna say yes.

19
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:54,780
It's just... I've been
so independent my whole life.

20
00:01:54,905 --> 00:01:57,992
- It's a big decision for me.
- I understand one hundred percent.

21
00:01:58,492 --> 00:02:01,037
Take your time.
There's no deadline.

22
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,831
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

23
00:02:04,665 --> 00:02:07,043
So, you gonna get onstage
and sing?

24
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:09,462
- Sorry.
- Uh...

25
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:11,005
Yeah.

26
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,885
- Jane, this better be important.
- "Yes, it is."

27
00:02:16,385 --> 00:02:21,223
I am heading south on trinity
between 6th and 7th.

28
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:24,769
- I need backup fast.
- W-what's going on?

29
00:02:27,104 --> 00:02:28,606
A girl's been abducted.

30
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:49,543
- What's going on?
- Okay, so...

31
00:02:51,962 --> 00:02:54,048
I went to buy some tacos
at that great truck on Juarez.

32
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:55,257
- You know the one?
- Yeah.

33
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:58,886
Anyhow, I bumped into this big
guy. He drops his shopping bags.

34
00:02:59,011 --> 00:03:03,474
And it's obvious from what spilled out
that he's keeping a woman captive.

35
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:06,852
So I followed him.
He went in there, in that guest house.

36
00:03:07,144 --> 00:03:09,939
Now, normally, I would take care of this
but this guy's sketchy.

37
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,149
What was in
the shopping bags?

38
00:03:12,274 --> 00:03:14,568
All sorts of stuff...
duct tape, women's vitamins.

39
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,696
You brought me out here
for duct tape?

40
00:03:16,987 --> 00:03:18,406
You need to trust me.

41
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:20,449
There is something off
about this guy.

42
00:03:20,574 --> 00:03:22,702
I mean, who buys nudie magazines
and tiger beat?

43
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:24,245
You know what?!
You're a jerk!

44
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:27,498
I was on a date, and you knew it
and you did this to screw it up.

45
00:03:27,623 --> 00:03:28,833
- You were on a date?
- Yeah.

46
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:31,961
And I am an idiot just for listening to you.
I'm gonna go see a band.

47
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:35,047
No, t-there is a woman in there
that doesn't wanna be

48
00:03:35,464 --> 00:03:38,300
and she's possibly injured,
all right?

49
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:41,011
I will bet you anything you like
that I am right.

50
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:43,347
I'll bet you
a million dollars.

51
00:03:44,932 --> 00:03:46,016
Fine.

52
00:03:59,947 --> 00:04:01,198
What?! What?!

53
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:04,368
Sir, we're with the FBI.
Do you have a female in there with you?

54
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:06,495
Female? No.

55
00:04:06,912 --> 00:04:10,416
No. No females.
No females here. I know you.

56
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:14,837
I know you. Don't lie to my friend.
She's a very serious person.

57
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:18,090
What's your problem, man?
I'm not lying.

58
00:04:19,967 --> 00:04:22,094
- Excuse me, sir.
- Hey! Y...

59
00:04:22,803 --> 00:04:26,015
This is agent Lisbon
with the FBI! Where are you?

60
00:04:27,224 --> 00:04:28,559
Stay there.

61
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:39,028
She's been shot.

62
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:41,238
Put your hands
on your head!

63
00:04:41,363 --> 00:04:43,908
- I-I didn't do nothing.
- Put them on your head!

64
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:46,994
She's really cold.

65
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:51,332
I need emergency medical
assistance at 812 Ashcroft.

66
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:53,083
It's a guest house
at the end of the drive.

67
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:55,669
I was tryna fix her.
T-that's why I went to the store.

68
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:56,962
Get down slowly.

69
00:04:57,087 --> 00:04:59,757
It's gonna be all right.
We have a doctor coming.

70
00:05:01,675 --> 00:05:03,761
I'm gonna get a doctor.
You're gonna be okay.

71
00:05:04,094 --> 00:05:06,764
Just look at me.
Look at me. I'm here.

72
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,641
Bow and arrow.

73
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,018
What does that mean,
"bow and arrow"?

74
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,062
I ain't speaking
no more.

75
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:15,397
Just look at me.
Breathe.

76
00:05:15,731 --> 00:05:19,735
It's okay.
Breathe, breathe.

77
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:22,613
Come on.

78
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,699
Just breathe.

79
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:29,745
Jane, she's gone.

80
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:43,175
Yeah, I know. I know.

81
00:06:02,359 --> 00:06:03,652
Mr. Delahay.

82
00:06:13,161 --> 00:06:17,165
{\an8}I need to understand how that girl
wound up in your bed, bleeding to death.

83
00:06:18,917 --> 00:06:22,671
{\an8}I was tryna make her better.
I didn't mean no harm.

84
00:06:23,463 --> 00:06:28,135
- Except you shot her, didn't you?
- No, I did not. I don't do that.

85
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,971
{\an8}I fix things...
things others throw away.

86
00:06:31,096 --> 00:06:32,431
{\an8}"I find new uses for them."

87
00:06:32,556 --> 00:06:34,308
"And I found her like that, and
I was gonna make her better"

88
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:35,601
"till you people interrupted."

89
00:06:35,726 --> 00:06:39,813
"She died because of you,
not because of me."

90
00:06:42,441 --> 00:06:44,443
Okay, well,
you say you found her.

91
00:06:45,152 --> 00:06:46,320
When was that?

92
00:06:46,445 --> 00:06:49,656
It was early last night
and I was out driving on route 16.

93
00:06:49,781 --> 00:06:51,033
That's how I find things, mostly.

94
00:06:51,158 --> 00:06:54,494
And that girl...
someone thought she was garbage.

95
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,371
But I knew better.

96
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:00,375
You have a history
of stalking girls, huh?

97
00:07:02,669 --> 00:07:04,880
Restraining orders
in Idaho and Nevada.

98
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:08,926
Now, that's lies and
bureaucracy, is what that is.

99
00:07:09,051 --> 00:07:10,636
I'm just...
I'm just trying...

100
00:07:15,057 --> 00:07:17,476
I didn't shoot nobody, never.

101
00:07:20,729 --> 00:07:24,524
{\an8}"Now, you say you found
this girl on route 16."

102
00:07:26,151 --> 00:07:27,194
Where exactly?

103
00:07:28,111 --> 00:07:29,237
{\an8}I don't know!

104
00:07:29,363 --> 00:07:31,365
{\an8}I don't remember!
I was drinking! I...

105
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:34,326
{\an8}I was... I was drunk.

106
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:38,664
Okay, well, if...
if we, uh, show you a map

107
00:07:39,206 --> 00:07:40,415
Would that help?

108
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,627
{\an8}Maps...
don't give me maps.

109
00:07:43,752 --> 00:07:45,462
{\an8}I know all about your maps.

110
00:07:54,262 --> 00:07:55,847
{\an8}That is one crazy individual.

111
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:57,808
He has no idea what he did.

112
00:07:58,225 --> 00:07:59,351
I think he does.

113
00:08:00,018 --> 00:08:04,189
{\an8}His world view is meticulously
constructed brick by brick.

114
00:08:04,982 --> 00:08:06,400
And we didn't find a gun.

115
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:09,319
{\an8}No registered weapon.
No gun in the house.

116
00:08:09,444 --> 00:08:11,405
{\an8}- No residue either.
- No.

117
00:08:12,531 --> 00:08:14,533
{\an8}But there was blood
in his truck.

118
00:08:16,326 --> 00:08:18,036
{\an8}So you think we should
believe his story?

119
00:08:18,745 --> 00:08:21,456
{\an8}A man goes for a drive
on route 16

120
00:08:21,581 --> 00:08:23,583
finds a gutshot girl,
and brings her home?

121
00:08:27,004 --> 00:08:29,589
{\an8}- Yeah.
- Yeah.

122
00:08:30,841 --> 00:08:34,428
Her name is Leanne Cole,
20 years old. We ran her fingerprints.

123
00:08:34,553 --> 00:08:37,681
{\an8}She was arrested for shoplifting
two years ago in Spokane.

124
00:08:37,806 --> 00:08:40,058
{\an8}She was also arrested for
driving with an expired license.

125
00:08:40,183 --> 00:08:42,102
{\an8}She tried to evade.
It was a misdemeanor.

126
00:08:42,227 --> 00:08:43,437
{\an8}So, joyriding.

127
00:08:43,937 --> 00:08:46,023
Looks like. Her parents died
when she was in high school.

128
00:08:46,189 --> 00:08:48,150
{\an8}Her aunt said
that she dropped out of school

129
00:08:48,275 --> 00:08:49,985
{\an8}And moved
down to Los Angeles.

130
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:52,779
I'm gonna go talk to her roommate
find out what she was doing in Texas.

131
00:08:55,157 --> 00:08:57,743
"What I don't get is how she got
back to the U.S. already."

132
00:08:58,076 --> 00:09:00,328
"They just left for Europe
four days ago."

133
00:09:00,579 --> 00:09:03,790
- For Europe.
- "Yeah. Like Italy and stuff."

134
00:09:03,915 --> 00:09:07,377
{\an8}- Who? Leanne and some guy?
- "Yeah, but it wasn't like that."

135
00:09:07,627 --> 00:09:09,296
{\an8}"Leanne wasn't a party girl."

136
00:09:09,796 --> 00:09:12,132
{\an8}"I know a lot of girls
who get taken all over."

137
00:09:12,632 --> 00:09:15,635
{\an8}"This was professional.
She booked a modeling gig."

138
00:09:15,761 --> 00:09:17,512
{\an8}And they left
four days ago?

139
00:09:17,637 --> 00:09:20,140
"Yeah. Some model scout
set it up."

140
00:09:20,432 --> 00:09:22,434
{\an8}Did you meet this guy...
the model scout?

141
00:09:22,559 --> 00:09:25,771
{\an8}"No, I didn't.
I think his name is Jesse."

142
00:09:28,106 --> 00:09:30,901
{\an8}No e-mails, no texts
with anyone named Jesse.

143
00:09:31,193 --> 00:09:32,778
And we're still waiting
on her phone records, right?

144
00:09:32,903 --> 00:09:34,279
Yeah, but here's the weird thing...

145
00:09:34,404 --> 00:09:36,114
She leaves for a modeling gig
four days ago

146
00:09:36,239 --> 00:09:38,366
and her digital life
just disappears... nothing.

147
00:09:38,492 --> 00:09:40,786
Delahay says he found her last night.
There's a three-day gap.

148
00:09:40,911 --> 00:09:44,539
So who was she with?
Where's this model scout?

149
00:09:44,664 --> 00:09:46,958
{\an8}Someone shot her and dumped her
on route 16.

150
00:09:47,084 --> 00:09:49,044
{\an8}- We don't even know where yet.
- We're working on that.

151
00:09:49,169 --> 00:09:50,670
{\an8}Jane's gonna jog
Delahay's memory.

152
00:09:53,673 --> 00:09:54,800
{\an8}Mind if I join you?

153
00:09:55,383 --> 00:09:56,718
Can't stop you.

154
00:09:57,177 --> 00:09:58,845
I can't even
scratch an itch.

155
00:10:01,681 --> 00:10:03,016
{\an8}Let me help you
with that.

156
00:10:04,476 --> 00:10:05,811
Let me see.

157
00:10:09,147 --> 00:10:11,066
All right.
Just hold still.

158
00:10:19,574 --> 00:10:20,826
Thank you.

159
00:10:22,452 --> 00:10:24,913
You say you don't remember
where you found Leanne Cole.

160
00:10:25,038 --> 00:10:26,331
I think
you do remember.

161
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,708
So you think I'm a liar, too.

162
00:10:28,834 --> 00:10:31,962
No. I just don't think
you can find the memory.

163
00:10:33,046 --> 00:10:34,089
Huh.

164
00:10:36,383 --> 00:10:37,509
Like beer?

165
00:10:38,802 --> 00:10:40,095
Who doesn't like beer?

166
00:10:43,515 --> 00:10:44,558
There you go.

167
00:10:55,527 --> 00:10:58,113
- Mm. That's good, huh?
- Mm-hmm.

168
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:04,244
Now, Thaddeus,
I want you to imagine

169
00:11:04,369 --> 00:11:07,080
that you're driving along
route 16 last night.

170
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,583
Okay.

171
00:11:11,793 --> 00:11:13,628
Might be easier
if you close your eyes.

172
00:11:20,177 --> 00:11:21,595
Now you're in your truck.

173
00:11:22,262 --> 00:11:25,640
Nice ice-cold beer
in the cupholder.

174
00:11:26,933 --> 00:11:29,019
You're about to turn
onto route 16.

175
00:11:29,769 --> 00:11:32,105
It's dark, warm.

176
00:11:33,732 --> 00:11:34,900
What do you hear?

177
00:11:35,442 --> 00:11:36,818
Jazz, man.

178
00:11:37,152 --> 00:11:39,446
Jazz on the radio, huh?

179
00:11:40,947 --> 00:11:42,616
You mind turning that down
a little?

180
00:11:46,286 --> 00:11:49,623
Thanks.
Now I can talk quietly.

181
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:53,710
The music's still playing.

182
00:11:54,336 --> 00:11:56,463
You're about to turn right
onto route 16.

183
00:11:56,588 --> 00:11:58,506
You can feel
the road change.

184
00:11:59,257 --> 00:12:00,759
Tell me what you see.

185
00:12:01,259 --> 00:12:05,764
Um... there's, uh...
Nothing at first.

186
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:09,851
Live oak tree on the right.

187
00:12:10,435 --> 00:12:12,729
Found an old miner's lamp there.

188
00:12:12,854 --> 00:12:15,273
Took it home, fixed it up.
Shh, shh, shh, shh.

189
00:12:15,398 --> 00:12:17,609
"I'm... I'm driving."

190
00:12:19,569 --> 00:12:20,654
"Yeah."

191
00:12:21,196 --> 00:12:24,616
"There... there's an old
gas station around mile two."

192
00:12:30,288 --> 00:12:32,249
"Turnoff for quint's farm."

193
00:12:33,124 --> 00:12:35,001
"They let me come
and haul stuff."

194
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:41,633
"A little creek...
But... It... it is dry now."

195
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:46,096
"Then... then,
there's an old bar."

196
00:12:47,555 --> 00:12:49,057
"It's empty now, and..."

197
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:54,688
- she's there.
- You can see her?

198
00:12:56,106 --> 00:13:00,026
She's all dusty, bleeding.

199
00:13:03,029 --> 00:13:05,240
"I-I... I can smell her hair."

200
00:13:07,575 --> 00:13:09,202
"It smells like dirt."

201
00:13:13,665 --> 00:13:14,874
Bingo.

202
00:13:17,627 --> 00:13:20,338
Hey.
What are you doing here?

203
00:13:20,463 --> 00:13:22,757
I got some Thai from that place
over on South Congress.

204
00:13:22,882 --> 00:13:25,051
- I love that place.
- I know.

205
00:13:25,510 --> 00:13:26,678
You're good.

206
00:13:26,803 --> 00:13:29,222
Mm... Not really.
I have an ulterior motive.

207
00:13:29,347 --> 00:13:32,142
- Oh?
- Just tryna make D.C. Look attractive.

208
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:34,185
Are they opening
a restaurant there?

209
00:13:34,311 --> 00:13:36,187
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Yeah.

210
00:13:36,313 --> 00:13:37,897
Hey, agent Pike.

211
00:13:38,773 --> 00:13:42,819
Ah! From your favorite Thai place
on South Congress. That's a shame.

212
00:13:43,445 --> 00:13:45,989
- Why?
- We gotta go. We have a location.

213
00:13:46,364 --> 00:13:48,408
- The girl?
- The girl.

214
00:13:48,533 --> 00:13:50,410
I'm driving.
I'll meet you downstairs.

215
00:13:56,666 --> 00:13:58,960
Oh, office scuttlebutt says
that your new guy

216
00:13:59,085 --> 00:14:02,339
is ditching us for the D.C. office
and maybe you're going with him.

217
00:14:02,630 --> 00:14:05,592
Oh. Well,
who told you about that?

218
00:14:06,801 --> 00:14:08,762
Well, you know,
I hear about things.

219
00:14:09,512 --> 00:14:11,848
Are you going with him?
We'd miss you.

220
00:14:12,223 --> 00:14:14,559
To be honest, sir,
I don't know.

221
00:14:15,143 --> 00:14:17,437
Hmm. What does Jane
have to say about this?

222
00:14:17,729 --> 00:14:19,439
Well, if he wants to talk
about it, he can.

223
00:14:19,564 --> 00:14:22,525
But he hasn't,
so I'm sure he's fine with it.

224
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:25,904
- Well, maybe he doesn't know.
- He's Jane. Of course he knows.

225
00:14:26,363 --> 00:14:29,449
- Remember, Jane is a psychic.
- A pretend psychic.

226
00:14:30,283 --> 00:14:32,786
If you haven't told him,
chances are he doesn't know.

227
00:15:15,245 --> 00:15:16,704
Delahay was driving east

228
00:15:16,830 --> 00:15:19,040
so he would have picked her up
on the south side of the street.

229
00:15:19,165 --> 00:15:20,917
So, south we should walk.

230
00:15:21,042 --> 00:15:22,627
Someone could have dumped
her from a truck.

231
00:15:22,752 --> 00:15:23,878
Or she was shot here.

232
00:15:24,003 --> 00:15:26,464
Her hair smelled of dirt.
Her shoes were caked in clay.

233
00:15:26,589 --> 00:15:29,426
She walked, collapsed.
He found her.

234
00:15:30,385 --> 00:15:32,512
We better be getting a move on.
This is wide-open country.

235
00:15:32,637 --> 00:15:34,889
Well, she was bleeding badly.
She couldn't have gone too far.

236
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:47,235
Voilà.

237
00:15:52,282 --> 00:15:53,616
Tractor trailer.

238
00:16:26,774 --> 00:16:30,361
Looks like some sort of way station
for undocumented immigrants.

239
00:16:30,653 --> 00:16:32,113
We're pretty far north for that.

240
00:16:34,699 --> 00:16:36,117
I'm gonna wait outside.

241
00:17:14,781 --> 00:17:15,949
Lisbon!

242
00:17:20,870 --> 00:17:22,372
- What?
- Shh, shh, shh, shh.

243
00:17:25,542 --> 00:17:26,709
Listen.

244
00:17:30,338 --> 00:17:31,548
You hear it?

245
00:17:35,593 --> 00:17:36,970
We need to move that.

246
00:17:58,866 --> 00:18:00,201
Oh, my God.

247
00:18:19,744 --> 00:18:22,580
Hey, Daniela.
You ready for me?

248
00:18:23,623 --> 00:18:24,832
I guess.

249
00:18:27,043 --> 00:18:28,461
Look, I know this is hard.

250
00:18:28,586 --> 00:18:31,923
But any detail you have
will help us find who did this to you.

251
00:18:32,965 --> 00:18:34,008
Can I sit?

252
00:18:39,931 --> 00:18:41,224
Did you find my sister?

253
00:18:42,308 --> 00:18:43,351
Your sister?

254
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:45,645
You have to find her.

255
00:18:49,273 --> 00:18:50,316
Is this her?

256
00:18:50,983 --> 00:18:52,068
No.

257
00:18:52,527 --> 00:18:56,030
- Do you recognize her?
- No. My sister's Amy Welker.

258
00:18:56,697 --> 00:18:58,783
She's 16.
You have to find her.

259
00:18:59,325 --> 00:19:02,245
- She was abducted with you?
- Yes.

260
00:19:03,079 --> 00:19:05,456
We're gonna do everything we can
to find your sister.

261
00:19:05,581 --> 00:19:07,208
You need to tell me
everything you know.

262
00:19:10,169 --> 00:19:11,212
Me and Amy...

263
00:19:12,088 --> 00:19:15,967
We did some modeling,
like little things, you know?

264
00:19:17,009 --> 00:19:19,971
We answered an ad online
for an open casting call.

265
00:19:21,389 --> 00:19:22,807
They took our head shots.

266
00:19:23,849 --> 00:19:25,518
The guy told us
to come back.

267
00:19:25,643 --> 00:19:29,021
- Wait. The photographer?
- No, the... the model scout.

268
00:19:30,064 --> 00:19:31,566
His name was Jesse.

269
00:19:32,316 --> 00:19:35,653
He said that clothing designers
in Europe

270
00:19:35,778 --> 00:19:37,405
would love us
for their shows.

271
00:19:38,531 --> 00:19:40,074
Did he say where
in Europe?

272
00:19:40,741 --> 00:19:41,826
No.

273
00:19:43,828 --> 00:19:46,080
He just said to bring
our passports and clothes

274
00:19:46,205 --> 00:19:48,082
and everything else
they'd take care of.

275
00:19:49,125 --> 00:19:50,835
Jesse gave us
a glass of champagne

276
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:54,171
and made a toast
to our new adventure together.

277
00:19:56,882 --> 00:20:00,845
Next thing...
I woke up.

278
00:20:02,763 --> 00:20:04,390
And I was in that place.

279
00:20:05,725 --> 00:20:07,643
One last question, Daniela.

280
00:20:08,019 --> 00:20:10,771
Do the words "bow and arrow"
mean anything to you?

281
00:20:11,397 --> 00:20:14,150
The girl we found said that
right before she died.

282
00:20:14,525 --> 00:20:17,069
Did Jesse ever say
those words to you?

283
00:20:17,612 --> 00:20:20,781
No. Why?

284
00:20:21,032 --> 00:20:23,618
Just asking.
It's okay.

285
00:20:26,954 --> 00:20:29,165
We're gonna do our best
to find your sister.

286
00:20:32,209 --> 00:20:34,253
Her sister was there.
There are more girls.

287
00:20:34,378 --> 00:20:35,921
- "We know."
- You know?

288
00:20:36,047 --> 00:20:37,923
Forensics is
at the safe house now.

289
00:20:38,382 --> 00:20:40,843
They found DNA from 20 different
people on those water bottles.

290
00:20:40,968 --> 00:20:42,553
- "20 girls?"
- Or more.

291
00:20:43,137 --> 00:20:46,265
She had the same story...
the phony model scout, this Jesse guy.

292
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,267
Someone is rounding up
these girls.

293
00:20:48,934 --> 00:20:51,562
Yeah. But where'd
they take them?

294
00:20:51,937 --> 00:20:55,566
We have approximately 20 young
females abducted by traffickers.

295
00:20:56,442 --> 00:20:58,861
We found fresh tractor-trailer
marks at the scene.

296
00:20:58,986 --> 00:21:02,490
So we figure these girls are on a truck
with an 18-hour head start on us.

297
00:21:02,615 --> 00:21:05,660
And since they're traffickers it's logical
to assume they headed to Mexico.

298
00:21:05,785 --> 00:21:07,870
Nuevo Laredo is where
they would most likely cross.

299
00:21:09,789 --> 00:21:13,209
The Laredo world trade port of entry.
Straight shot down I-35.

300
00:21:13,334 --> 00:21:15,336
But the truck left
at least 18 hours ago.

301
00:21:15,461 --> 00:21:17,546
Which means they could be a thousand
miles into Mexico by now.

302
00:21:17,672 --> 00:21:19,882
- Possible but not probable.
- No?

303
00:21:20,049 --> 00:21:22,593
Well, when the truck left the house
it was headed due north, right?

304
00:21:22,718 --> 00:21:25,554
So, uh, last time I looked,
Mexico was the other way.

305
00:21:25,846 --> 00:21:27,723
So, you think
they're headed to Oklahoma?

306
00:21:27,848 --> 00:21:30,267
That's not exactly a hot spot
for sex-slave trafficking.

307
00:21:30,393 --> 00:21:32,937
True, so they headed north
for some other reason...

308
00:21:33,229 --> 00:21:35,690
- Pick up more girls, probably.
- It's possible.

309
00:21:36,148 --> 00:21:38,901
Yeah, you can fit a lot more
than 20 girls in a freight container.

310
00:21:39,026 --> 00:21:40,695
More like 40.
But not for long.

311
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:43,906
So by now, they're probably
headed south to Mexico

312
00:21:44,031 --> 00:21:46,742
straight down the I-35,
probably as we speak...

313
00:21:46,867 --> 00:21:47,993
Well, possibly.

314
00:21:48,327 --> 00:21:50,496
Too thin to warrant
closing down a highway.

315
00:21:50,621 --> 00:21:52,915
And that's what we would need
in order to search every truck.

316
00:21:53,374 --> 00:21:55,000
Hmm. Yeah.

317
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:58,629
Well, we don't need to set up
a real road block.

318
00:22:00,047 --> 00:22:03,134
We just need to convince the driver
of that truck that we've set up a roadblock.

319
00:22:08,597 --> 00:22:11,183
Sorry... scanning long-range
frequencies is like...

320
00:22:14,854 --> 00:22:17,940
- I don't have a metaphor. It's hard.
- "Heads up on a 10-42."

321
00:22:18,065 --> 00:22:21,819
"Traffic jam's backed up across
the border there at Nuevo Laredo."

322
00:22:21,944 --> 00:22:23,320
"Thanks a lot, Heavy Metal."

323
00:22:25,197 --> 00:22:26,532
Places, everyone.

324
00:22:28,409 --> 00:22:29,952
"This is lefty here.
Heads up."

325
00:22:30,077 --> 00:22:33,956
"I'm hearing highway patrol set up
a checkpoint right near the border on I-35."

326
00:22:34,081 --> 00:22:35,291
Over.

327
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:44,341
"Yep. They pulled me over,
checked my cab and my cargo."

328
00:22:44,467 --> 00:22:47,928
"And these aren't county Mounties.
These are some full-grown bears."

329
00:22:55,770 --> 00:22:57,730
"Big Pete jumping in
with a 10-17."

330
00:22:57,855 --> 00:22:59,982
"Company driver said smokey's
set up on the southbound side"

331
00:23:00,107 --> 00:23:01,358
"about yardstick 21."

332
00:23:01,484 --> 00:23:03,986
"They eyeballed him, but he's deadheading
so they waved him through."

333
00:23:06,155 --> 00:23:07,239
What?

334
00:23:11,660 --> 00:23:12,912
That was incredible.

335
00:23:14,413 --> 00:23:16,540
"10-4, big Pete.
Thanks for the heads up."

336
00:23:16,665 --> 00:23:18,334
"I'll pass that along.
Over."

337
00:23:19,543 --> 00:23:22,671
I believe you hooked him, big Pete.
I believe you hooked him.

338
00:23:23,214 --> 00:23:25,341
I'm gonna pull off at that diner
right north of Laredo

339
00:23:25,466 --> 00:23:28,219
and make sure the cab's shipshape
before I hit that bear trap.

340
00:23:43,943 --> 00:23:45,736
- It's crowded.
- Yes, it is.

341
00:23:47,905 --> 00:23:50,491
- How do we know if it worked?
- Oh, it worked.

342
00:23:50,616 --> 00:23:53,285
You think all these people got off the roads
because they're scared of cops?

343
00:23:53,410 --> 00:23:55,579
Well, not all of them.
Just the ones that have something to hide.

344
00:23:55,704 --> 00:23:57,331
Well, how can we tell
which one's our driver?

345
00:23:57,456 --> 00:23:58,499
We look.

346
00:24:11,178 --> 00:24:13,722
- What about those two?
- The lady? I don't think so.

347
00:24:14,473 --> 00:24:16,475
Not just her.
The two of them.

348
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:18,352
They're obviously
traveling together.

349
00:24:18,477 --> 00:24:20,354
They're not a couple.
There's no intimacy there.

350
00:24:20,479 --> 00:24:23,023
Oh, they've been in a truck for hours.
How could there be intimacy?

351
00:24:23,148 --> 00:24:24,316
I'll show you.

352
00:24:29,572 --> 00:24:31,323
- Ohh!
- Oh, sorry.

353
00:24:36,579 --> 00:24:37,621
What was that about?

354
00:24:37,746 --> 00:24:40,457
Well, I bumped her, and he didn't
say anything. They're not a couple.

355
00:24:47,172 --> 00:24:48,799
He's got a gun in his jacket.

356
00:25:09,445 --> 00:25:10,779
Go get them, guys.

357
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:42,394
You okay?

358
00:26:05,918 --> 00:26:08,587
- FBI!
- Cut your engine!

359
00:26:10,005 --> 00:26:11,215
Lady!

360
00:26:27,314 --> 00:26:30,109
It's all right, ladies. We're
with the FBI. You're safe now.

361
00:26:53,230 --> 00:26:54,439
Hi, Daniela.

362
00:26:54,564 --> 00:26:56,608
I'm special agent Kimball Cho
with the FBI.

363
00:26:57,567 --> 00:27:00,487
We just stopped a truck that was
transporting girls into Mexico.

364
00:27:00,612 --> 00:27:01,863
Was my sister on it?

365
00:27:02,114 --> 00:27:03,740
No, I'm sorry.
We didn't find your sister.

366
00:27:03,865 --> 00:27:05,325
But we're still looking.
Don't worry.

367
00:27:05,450 --> 00:27:06,701
Now, I've interviewed the girls
from the truck

368
00:27:06,827 --> 00:27:09,496
and their descriptions match yours
regarding the modeling scam.

369
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:12,541
We've made a composite sketch
from your description and theirs

370
00:27:12,666 --> 00:27:13,834
of the modelling scout.

371
00:27:15,001 --> 00:27:16,837
Does this look like the man
you and your sister met with?

372
00:27:17,838 --> 00:27:20,799
Yes!
That's Jesse.

373
00:27:20,924 --> 00:27:23,552
Okay. Thank you.
It's a big help.

374
00:27:24,344 --> 00:27:25,387
Agent Cho!

375
00:27:26,763 --> 00:27:28,223
Find my sister, please.

376
00:27:30,642 --> 00:27:33,270
- She's just a kid.
- Okay.

377
00:27:45,574 --> 00:27:48,076
Are the girls all right?
Are they safe?

378
00:27:50,620 --> 00:27:52,455
Do you recognize
either of those girls?

379
00:27:53,540 --> 00:27:54,583
No.

380
00:27:56,251 --> 00:27:58,712
That's Amy Welker.
She's 16 years old.

381
00:28:02,799 --> 00:28:04,509
She might have been
on the other truck.

382
00:28:04,634 --> 00:28:07,679
- The other truck?
- Yeah. They left the day before we did.

383
00:28:08,471 --> 00:28:10,473
Those girls are
well over the border by now.

384
00:28:10,765 --> 00:28:12,601
- Who is the driver?
- I never met him.

385
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:16,188
What happened to the girls
after they were delivered?

386
00:28:16,313 --> 00:28:17,355
I don't know.

387
00:28:19,357 --> 00:28:22,319
I'm not a bad person.
I really need you to believe that.

388
00:28:22,652 --> 00:28:23,778
Why should I?

389
00:28:25,906 --> 00:28:28,450
The bank was gonna foreclose
on my parents' house

390
00:28:29,075 --> 00:28:31,953
so I agreed to drive
some illegals over the border.

391
00:28:32,078 --> 00:28:33,622
It didn't seem so bad,
you know?

392
00:28:34,456 --> 00:28:36,750
- It's still against the law.
- I know

393
00:28:37,125 --> 00:28:39,628
and that's what I said,
too, after the one trip.

394
00:28:39,961 --> 00:28:42,589
They told me they'd
turn me over to the police

395
00:28:42,714 --> 00:28:46,718
unless I started driving trucks
full of girls the other way into Mexico.

396
00:28:47,260 --> 00:28:48,887
How did you get the girls
over the border?

397
00:28:49,471 --> 00:28:51,348
A border guard...
he'd been paid off.

398
00:28:51,932 --> 00:28:53,934
- He'd recognize the truck.
- How?

399
00:28:54,517 --> 00:28:56,811
There's a dashboard ornament
in my cab.

400
00:28:57,145 --> 00:28:59,272
It was provided
by the guys in Mexico...

401
00:28:59,898 --> 00:29:01,233
A hula dancer.

402
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:06,279
What about the girl
who ran off... Leanne Cole.

403
00:29:07,197 --> 00:29:09,908
- She got away?
- She's dead.

404
00:29:10,617 --> 00:29:12,494
I was really hoping
she got away.

405
00:29:16,915 --> 00:29:18,083
We were running late.

406
00:29:19,125 --> 00:29:20,669
"Ramon was pissed."

407
00:29:22,003 --> 00:29:23,046
Please!

408
00:29:24,881 --> 00:29:28,802
Get in there. It's okay. It's okay.
You're doing good. You're doing good.

409
00:29:28,927 --> 00:29:30,845
We're 45 minutes behind!
What the hell, Claudia?!

410
00:29:30,971 --> 00:29:33,765
Relax, Ramon.
We'll make it up on the road.

411
00:29:34,474 --> 00:29:35,850
Come on! Speed it up!

412
00:29:49,197 --> 00:29:52,033
- Claudia, go get her!
- Me?!

413
00:29:52,284 --> 00:29:53,660
Go!

414
00:29:57,455 --> 00:30:00,417
Go find her now!
Come on!

415
00:30:07,841 --> 00:30:09,801
- Where is she?
- I don't know!

416
00:30:10,343 --> 00:30:11,511
I don't see her.

417
00:30:13,138 --> 00:30:14,264
We're an hour behind.

418
00:30:15,849 --> 00:30:17,475
Get to the truck.
Come on. We gotta go.

419
00:30:18,893 --> 00:30:21,730
He started making calls,
telling people what happened.

420
00:30:21,896 --> 00:30:23,565
- Who did he call?
- I don't know.

421
00:30:23,690 --> 00:30:25,608
But I never saw him so scared.

422
00:30:26,109 --> 00:30:27,819
He was worried
she'd go to the police?

423
00:30:27,944 --> 00:30:30,989
No. Ramon wasn't scared
of the cops.

424
00:30:31,114 --> 00:30:34,242
It was the guy he worked for
that scared the hell out of him.

425
00:30:34,367 --> 00:30:36,661
- Do you know his name?
- I just know Ramon

426
00:30:36,786 --> 00:30:38,997
and the guys
we turned the girls over to.

427
00:30:39,122 --> 00:30:40,373
Did you get their names?

428
00:30:40,498 --> 00:30:44,669
Yeah. The Qasimi brothers,
Ali and Ray.

429
00:30:45,295 --> 00:30:47,172
This is Ray and Ali Qasimi.

430
00:30:47,672 --> 00:30:50,592
They're businessmen with
connections to the Middle East and Asia.

431
00:30:51,092 --> 00:30:55,555
Raised and Educated in the U.S.
they have a network of assets worldwide.

432
00:30:56,222 --> 00:30:59,392
I checked with Washington,
put in a call to Interpol

433
00:30:59,517 --> 00:31:01,478
and there's nothing
on these guys.

434
00:31:01,603 --> 00:31:02,854
They're as clean
as a whistle.

435
00:31:04,105 --> 00:31:05,648
How are we doing with the leads
from the girls?

436
00:31:05,774 --> 00:31:08,735
The modeling agencies all pulled
up stakes after Ramon's call.

437
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:10,487
All that's left
are empty storefronts.

438
00:31:10,612 --> 00:31:12,864
We're tryna track backwards
through phone records

439
00:31:12,989 --> 00:31:15,825
and rental agreements
but I don't think we're gonna get much.

440
00:31:15,992 --> 00:31:17,744
It was
a well-run organization.

441
00:31:17,994 --> 00:31:20,580
Okay, what about Ramon's cellphone?
Is there anything that we can use?

442
00:31:20,955 --> 00:31:22,248
It was a prepaid cell.

443
00:31:22,374 --> 00:31:24,501
All the calls he made
went to burner phones, as well.

444
00:31:25,168 --> 00:31:26,211
Okay.

445
00:31:27,128 --> 00:31:29,923
Does anyone have any good news
that they can offer up?

446
00:31:30,173 --> 00:31:32,092
Well, all the women ID'd
the same model agent.

447
00:31:32,217 --> 00:31:34,219
Called himself Jesse.
We had a drawing made.

448
00:31:34,344 --> 00:31:36,596
Wylie's running it through
the facial-recognition database.

449
00:31:36,721 --> 00:31:38,723
Um, I think I just got a hit, actually.

450
00:31:38,848 --> 00:31:40,892
There's a James O'connor
in San Diego

451
00:31:41,017 --> 00:31:43,353
Who's a really close match...
also goes by Jesse.

452
00:31:43,478 --> 00:31:44,646
I'm sending cops
to check on him.

453
00:31:44,771 --> 00:31:46,398
Okay. Well, that's good news.
Anyone else?

454
00:31:47,148 --> 00:31:48,650
Can't we bring
the Qasimis in?

455
00:31:48,775 --> 00:31:50,443
The driver will testify
against them.

456
00:31:50,735 --> 00:31:53,863
They're in Mexico with no criminal record
and a ticking clock.

457
00:31:54,030 --> 00:31:56,783
By the time we get an extradition order
they'll be long gone.

458
00:31:56,908 --> 00:31:58,910
And I don't think we can get them
to come to the states for us.

459
00:31:59,202 --> 00:32:02,163
- Do we still have the driver's truck?
- Yeah. It's impounded.

460
00:32:02,455 --> 00:32:05,667
But according to the Qasimis,
it's just late.

461
00:32:06,376 --> 00:32:08,711
- I bet they're getting anxious now.
- And?

462
00:32:09,254 --> 00:32:12,090
- Well, that's our in.
- How's that?

463
00:32:12,215 --> 00:32:14,217
You and I are gonna drive
that truck down to Mexico

464
00:32:14,342 --> 00:32:17,512
and we're gonna talk those Qasimis
into doing a deal with us.

465
00:32:17,637 --> 00:32:19,389
I don't think
that's a good idea.

466
00:32:19,514 --> 00:32:21,683
I do.
What do you say?

467
00:32:30,984 --> 00:32:32,735
Maybe this wasn't
such a good idea.

468
00:32:33,987 --> 00:32:36,322
No. I think
it looks good on you.

469
00:32:37,949 --> 00:32:40,118
I like it.
Stylish, but manly.

470
00:32:42,537 --> 00:32:43,955
What?
You wanna try mine?

471
00:32:45,123 --> 00:32:46,708
That's not what I was...

472
00:32:47,584 --> 00:32:49,127
You're not getting this.

473
00:32:50,837 --> 00:32:52,172
Never mind.

474
00:33:06,209 --> 00:33:08,753
"There's a free-trade zone just
south of the border into Mexico."

475
00:33:08,878 --> 00:33:09,921
"Nafta created it."

476
00:33:10,046 --> 00:33:12,423
"No tariffs, cheap materials,
cheap labor..."

477
00:33:12,548 --> 00:33:13,800
"Products for the U.S. Market."

478
00:33:14,050 --> 00:33:15,551
Now, the Qasimis own
a factory there.

479
00:33:15,676 --> 00:33:16,719
That's where the girls
were dropped off

480
00:33:16,844 --> 00:33:18,513
and then shipped out
to their new destinations

481
00:33:18,638 --> 00:33:20,098
probably somewhere
in the Middle East.

482
00:33:20,390 --> 00:33:21,974
Now, the Qasimis appear legit

483
00:33:22,517 --> 00:33:24,560
but that doesn't mean they won't
have muscle at the factory.

484
00:33:24,685 --> 00:33:26,979
Well, it's the border.
They'll have muscle.

485
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:29,899
"We're counting on that.
The Qasimis are smart."

486
00:33:30,191 --> 00:33:33,444
"If we arrest them, they'll flip on whoever's
rounding up these girls in the U.S."

487
00:33:33,861 --> 00:33:35,446
"that's the guy
we need to find."

488
00:33:44,288 --> 00:33:47,250
You wanna give that to your bosses and tell
them we'd like to have a little chat?

489
00:34:05,059 --> 00:34:07,937
Howdy. Uh, my name is,
uh, Patrick.

490
00:34:08,187 --> 00:34:09,647
This is my head of security, Dennis.

491
00:34:09,856 --> 00:34:11,941
You all must be, uh,
Ray and Ali.

492
00:34:13,818 --> 00:34:14,902
Ray and Ali?

493
00:34:15,027 --> 00:34:17,822
We don't know you.
Where did you get that?

494
00:34:19,365 --> 00:34:22,201
Well, I own a couple of
gentlemen's clubs up in Houston.

495
00:34:22,493 --> 00:34:25,079
Real exclusive...
you know, o-only the best.

496
00:34:25,204 --> 00:34:27,540
Ramon...
he likes coming into my club.

497
00:34:27,665 --> 00:34:28,875
He likes my girls.

498
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,585
He likes them all the way
to the poorhouse.

499
00:34:31,794 --> 00:34:32,837
Who's Ramon?

500
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:36,382
I gotcha.

501
00:34:36,716 --> 00:34:38,259
Uh, mum's the word, huh?

502
00:34:38,384 --> 00:34:42,138
Here's the thing... Ramon gave me the truck
that this here gal came from.

503
00:34:44,140 --> 00:34:46,517
Uh, this Ramon,
whoever he is...

504
00:34:47,018 --> 00:34:50,062
Why would he do that...
just give you a truck?

505
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:53,357
Ramon had a little bit
of bad luck.

506
00:34:54,066 --> 00:34:55,193
One of them girls ran off.

507
00:34:55,318 --> 00:34:57,987
He thought he might have winged
her, but he never did find her.

508
00:34:58,571 --> 00:35:01,949
And he got to thinking
that maybe the man in charge

509
00:35:02,742 --> 00:35:04,202
would take it all amiss.

510
00:35:04,327 --> 00:35:06,287
I figure
you guys know that man.

511
00:35:07,038 --> 00:35:08,539
That's none
of your business.

512
00:35:10,750 --> 00:35:13,294
- Continue.
- Ramon was scared.

513
00:35:14,045 --> 00:35:15,922
He wanted to take
a long holiday.

514
00:35:16,464 --> 00:35:19,008
Needed some cash,
so I obliged.

515
00:35:19,133 --> 00:35:22,678
And in return, he gave me
that truck and all its cargo.

516
00:35:26,974 --> 00:35:28,309
Is the cargo safe?

517
00:35:28,893 --> 00:35:30,436
Well, a little weepy maybe.

518
00:35:30,978 --> 00:35:33,189
Lot of runny makeup.
But sure, it's safe.

519
00:35:34,273 --> 00:35:36,984
Well, suppose,
just for kicks

520
00:35:37,902 --> 00:35:39,320
that we know Ramon

521
00:35:39,612 --> 00:35:41,864
and we want that truck
and the cargo.

522
00:35:43,074 --> 00:35:44,242
How much?

523
00:35:45,034 --> 00:35:47,161
10 thou for the truck,
5 thou a head.

524
00:35:48,871 --> 00:35:51,707
Come on. They're girls,
not racehorses.

525
00:35:52,959 --> 00:35:54,877
- $1,000 a head.
- 3 thou.

526
00:35:55,002 --> 00:35:56,712
- $2,000.
- Deal.

527
00:35:57,129 --> 00:35:59,006
But you got to come across
the border and pick it up.

528
00:35:59,131 --> 00:36:00,424
- No.
- No.

529
00:36:00,550 --> 00:36:01,759
You deliver them to us.

530
00:36:02,093 --> 00:36:03,386
No. No deal.

531
00:36:03,970 --> 00:36:06,055
I'm a businessman.
I ain't no smuggler.

532
00:36:06,639 --> 00:36:08,683
You want that truck,
you want its cargo

533
00:36:08,808 --> 00:36:10,726
You come across the border,
and you pick it up.

534
00:36:29,537 --> 00:36:30,788
How much further?

535
00:36:31,956 --> 00:36:33,374
We're almost there now.

536
00:36:50,850 --> 00:36:52,184
There she blows.

537
00:36:58,941 --> 00:37:00,067
Give us the keys.

538
00:37:00,192 --> 00:37:02,361
Sure.
Give me the money first.

539
00:37:11,954 --> 00:37:14,332
- Whoa. That's ain't money.
- No, it's not.

540
00:37:17,251 --> 00:37:19,712
I thought we were just businessmen.
This is business, right?

541
00:37:19,837 --> 00:37:21,213
It's a tough business.

542
00:37:36,896 --> 00:37:38,189
There's nothing in there.

543
00:37:39,815 --> 00:37:42,151
FBI! You're under arrest!
Get down on the ground!

544
00:37:42,276 --> 00:37:43,861
Get down on the ground!
Right there!

545
00:37:43,986 --> 00:37:45,029
Get down!

546
00:37:46,280 --> 00:37:47,365
Yeah.

547
00:37:47,490 --> 00:37:49,700
Yeah, you're right.
It's a tough business, isn't it?

548
00:37:55,498 --> 00:37:57,958
- You look uncomfortable.
- Don't be.

549
00:37:58,084 --> 00:37:59,377
We're here to help you.

550
00:37:59,502 --> 00:38:01,420
Help?
You've killed me.

551
00:38:01,754 --> 00:38:05,216
Just by bringing us here
my brother and I are already dead.

552
00:38:05,508 --> 00:38:08,010
We're just about the only people
who can help you now.

553
00:38:08,135 --> 00:38:11,847
No. You have no idea
who you're dealing with.

554
00:38:11,972 --> 00:38:14,642
You people are amateurs
compared to him.

555
00:38:14,767 --> 00:38:16,727
Who? Give us a name.

556
00:38:18,312 --> 00:38:19,814
He will bury you.

557
00:38:20,314 --> 00:38:23,359
- Well, we'll see about that.
- Yeah, you will.

558
00:38:27,655 --> 00:38:31,033
You recognize this girl?
She's 16 years old.

559
00:38:33,536 --> 00:38:35,413
My brother and me
will not say a word.

560
00:38:37,039 --> 00:38:39,667
Maybe some time in gen pop
will loosen their tongues.

561
00:38:39,792 --> 00:38:41,377
Maybe, but I don't
have high hopes.

562
00:38:41,502 --> 00:38:42,878
I better go tell Daniela.

563
00:38:43,587 --> 00:38:45,047
San Diego police
are on the line.

564
00:38:45,589 --> 00:38:46,757
Put it on speaker.

565
00:38:49,969 --> 00:38:52,263
This is agent Cho. You're
calling about Jesse O'connor?

566
00:38:52,388 --> 00:38:54,974
"Yes, sir, but I'm sorry to tell
you we don't have good news."

567
00:38:55,141 --> 00:38:56,809
- He wasn't there?
- "No, sir. He was there."

568
00:38:56,976 --> 00:38:58,811
"Only thing is,
somebody else got him first."

569
00:38:58,936 --> 00:39:00,396
- He's dead?
- "Yes, sir."

570
00:39:00,521 --> 00:39:03,149
"Throat cut ear to ear.
I'm sending you a picture."

571
00:39:15,119 --> 00:39:18,247
Thank you, officer. Please keep us
in the loop on your investigation.

572
00:39:19,415 --> 00:39:20,458
Thanks. Bye.

573
00:39:29,717 --> 00:39:30,843
You okay?

574
00:39:39,643 --> 00:39:42,772
- Hello. Yes?
- "That thing in San Diego?"

575
00:39:42,897 --> 00:39:44,440
"It's taken care of,
just so you know."

576
00:39:44,774 --> 00:39:46,150
Jesse O'connor,
you mean?

577
00:39:46,275 --> 00:39:49,236
Yep. He won't be an issue
for you anymore.

578
00:39:49,904 --> 00:39:52,615
Good. Now we have another
problem I need you to fix.

579
00:39:53,407 --> 00:39:54,450
Oh, yeah?

580
00:39:54,867 --> 00:39:55,910
"The Qasimis."

581
00:39:56,368 --> 00:39:58,454
A similar solution
would be greatly appreciated.

582
00:39:58,954 --> 00:40:01,290
You got it, Mr. Ridley.
How soon you need it done?

583
00:40:01,415 --> 00:40:03,042
Time is of the essence, Anthony.

584
00:40:03,751 --> 00:40:05,711
Time is of the essence.

585
00:40:06,212 --> 00:40:07,296
Okay.

586
00:40:14,303 --> 00:40:15,846
"We didn't find your sister."

587
00:40:16,555 --> 00:40:18,808
There was another truck.
She may have been on that.

588
00:40:19,141 --> 00:40:21,936
So someone saw her
at the house?

589
00:40:22,561 --> 00:40:24,647
Maybe.
We can't be sure.

590
00:40:25,397 --> 00:40:28,317
But you will find her
and catch whoever's left, right?

591
00:40:29,568 --> 00:40:31,445
You'll punish them
for what they've done?

592
00:40:31,570 --> 00:40:32,655
We will.

593
00:40:33,739 --> 00:40:35,032
I promise.

594
00:40:35,157 --> 00:40:37,159
Well, she promised,
so now we have to.

595
00:40:40,079 --> 00:40:41,997
"You, uh, need me to give you
a ride someplace?"

596
00:40:42,122 --> 00:40:43,833
Oh, no, that's all right.
I already got one.

597
00:40:48,838 --> 00:40:50,297
He was just waiting there
all the time?

598
00:40:50,422 --> 00:40:51,507
Yeah.

599
00:40:51,924 --> 00:40:54,343
Well, I guess those art-department guys
aren't that busy, huh?

600
00:40:54,468 --> 00:40:57,179
It's the art-crimes department,
and he's very busy.

601
00:40:57,304 --> 00:40:59,306
He just makes a point
to be there for me.

602
00:41:03,727 --> 00:41:05,187
You really like this guy, huh?

603
00:41:07,022 --> 00:41:08,816
He got a promotion.

604
00:41:08,941 --> 00:41:11,110
It's a-a posting in D.C.

605
00:41:12,319 --> 00:41:14,446
and he asked me
to go with him

606
00:41:14,572 --> 00:41:16,699
So we can be together in D.C.

607
00:41:17,867 --> 00:41:19,159
I'm thinking about it.

608
00:41:20,244 --> 00:41:21,495
Yeah.

609
00:41:24,290 --> 00:41:25,457
Hmm.

610
00:41:26,876 --> 00:41:29,169
What do you think
about it?

611
00:41:30,421 --> 00:41:32,965
Uh... I mean...

612
00:41:33,507 --> 00:41:35,175
Congratulations, I guess.

613
00:41:36,844 --> 00:41:38,304
Congratulations?

614
00:41:38,762 --> 00:41:40,180
That's all
you're gonna say?

615
00:41:41,891 --> 00:41:46,103
Sure. Well, I mean, if... if...
if that's... If that's what you want.

616
00:41:46,437 --> 00:41:48,606
- You're not upset?
- No. Of course not.

617
00:41:48,731 --> 00:41:51,150
I mean, if that's, um...
if you're happy.

618
00:41:51,275 --> 00:41:52,526
Oh, I'm happy.

619
00:41:53,444 --> 00:41:54,653
Then I'm happy.

620
00:41:57,156 --> 00:41:59,366
- Hey.
- Hi.

621
00:41:59,491 --> 00:42:01,952
Guess what. That show
we missed the other night...

622
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:03,954
They're playing another one
in 45 minutes.

623
00:42:04,079 --> 00:42:06,332
We can catch it if... if...
you guys are done here, right?

624
00:42:06,457 --> 00:42:08,250
- Oh, we're done. Yeah.
- Yeah. Sure.

625
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:11,462
- See you, Patrick.
- See you.

